WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:01.601
What about

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.135
the legal

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.336
battle between Florida

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.405
Governor Ron DeSantis and Disney?

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.040
You said you would happily

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.508
welcome Disney to South Carolina

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.043
if they wanted to move.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.378
What do you think of Governor

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:12.312
DeSantis, his leadership

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:13.480
when it comes to the back

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.748
and forth with Disney?

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:15.148
Well, it's

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.716
the hypocrisy of the whole thing.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:17.751
What I said was,

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:19.819
first of all, this all started with

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.888
the don't say gay bill, right.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.757
And it basically said

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:24.357
you couldn't

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:24.958
talk about

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.259
gender to any child

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.994
before the third grade.

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.462
I have been on record saying,

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.297
I don't think that went far enough.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.199
They should not be talking to our kids

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:34.367
about gender, period.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.268
That's what parents

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.369
talk to their kids about.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.271
Not in school

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.777
So let's put that bill away

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:44.744
and put that to the side.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.179
I totally agree with the bill

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.614
and think that it needed to go further.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.716
And I think they've done that since then.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.051
What I'm talking about

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.819
is the fact that here

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:55.088
you have a woke company,

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:56.723
even woke for years.

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.324
I remember when Disney went after

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.193
President Trump for immigration.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.395
This is nothing new.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.397
So here you have DeSantis,

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.399
who accepted 50,000

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:09.002
political contributions from Disney

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.770
He went and put their executives

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.971
and their lobbyists

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:14.074
on prominent boards throughout Florida,

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:15.608
and he went

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.576
and basically

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.278
gave the highest corporate

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:21.047
subsidies in Florida history to Disney.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:24.751
But because they went and criticized him,

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:26.086
now he's going to spend

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:28.321
taxpayer dollars on a lawsuit

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:31.124
It's just like all this vendetta stuff.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.559
We've been down that road again.

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.727
We can't go down that.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.196
Businesses were my partners

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:37.130
in South Carolina.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.099
We didn't always get along.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:39.599
And I

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:40.266
you know,

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.769
luckily South Carolina's very anti woke.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.038
But when you have a company like that,

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.606
don't bring the citizens

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.308
taxpayer dollars into it.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.242
Pick up the phone,

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:50.477
deal with it, settle it

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:51.544
the way you should.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.179
And I just think he's being hypocritical.

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:54.013
And publican

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:54.581
and presidential

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:54.881
hopeful

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:55.482
Nikki Haley

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:57.217
drawing a clear distinction

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:57.784
from her main

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:58.618
rivals,

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.986
Donald Trump and Governor Ron

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:02.021
DeSantis during a CNN town hall.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:02.655
Joining us now,

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.390
CNN senior political commentator

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.024
Scott Jennings

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.559
and CNN political commentator

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.495
and attorney Bakari Sellers.

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:10.163
Good morning. Welcome to you both.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.131
I think let's just start

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.599
with coming off of that town hall.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:12.832
I mean,

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.167
how do you do from your perspective?

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.301
Was it a good night for her?

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:16.936
I thought she's a very

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.404
polished presentation.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.073
You know, she may be the most polished

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.441
politician in the field.

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:22.041
The question is,

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.309
is that what people are looking for?

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.078
That is the question these days.

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:26.646
And, you know, she

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.748
she had some great moments on Russia.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.049
I think I like some of the honesty

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.985
she had on a few issues.

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:33.019
She does engage

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.221
in a lot of the normal political pablum

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.823
that sort of is out of vogue right now

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.525
in the Trump era.

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:39.192
But overall,

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:40.260
I thought it was a pretty good night.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.194
She passed the test

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.529
and we'll see if that makes a difference

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:43.496
in her polling car.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.130
You know,

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.498
Nikki Haley, I mean, you have

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.399
you were in elected office

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.167
at the same time.

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.067
I mean, is this a stand

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:48.668
beside each other?

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:49.369
Not at the same desk,

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:50.003
but beside each other

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.437
for about four years.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.805
And we're from the same home county.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.140
So shout out to Bamberg County, where

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.775
we're punching above our weight

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:56.809
this morning.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.578
But Nikki Haley, I'd say this to vote

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.213
for a long period of time.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.381
She's probably the most talented

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.782
politician in the country.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.017
I say that with no hesitation.

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:04.817
She's very skilled.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:05.385
She's very good.

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:05.618
One on

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.453
one in these small retail settings,

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:08.121
which is going to bode

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:08.821
well in places

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.023
like Iowa and New Hampshire

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:12.258
and even back at home in South Carolina.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.126
The problem that Nikki

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:13.793
Haley has is

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.728
nobody really knows what she stands for

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:16.262
and I'm not sure

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.897
she clarified that last night.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.499
You saw many of the inconsistencies.

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:21.067
And sometimes politicians,

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:21.801
including myself,

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.536
we try to get too cute by half

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:25.271
and we begin to weave in and weave out.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.040
And sometimes we just make no sense.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:27.774
You saw that on things

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:28.374
like abortion

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:28.908
where she didn't

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.109
want to be nailed down,

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.878
where she signed a 20 week abortion

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:32.879
bill in South Carolina,

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:35.248
with the exception for life of the mother

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.150
but no exception for rape and incest.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.418
She didn't really want to talk about that

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:38.885
last night.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:39.719
She didn't want to talk about

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.387
whether or not she would sign

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.556
her successor six week abortion plan.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:44.757
So when you think about these things,

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.259
you see it was a little bit uneven.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.894
She was extremely strong

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:48.361
to Scott's

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.829
point on issues that she knows

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.731
really well on Afghanistan,

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.800
on Russia, on foreign policy.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.134
When she got in, woke ism

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.937
and the cultural politics of the day,

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.806
you saw she was really uncomfortable.

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:00.707
Let's play

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:01.441
what she said

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:02.342
about Ukraine

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:04.544
and Western support for Ukraine.

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:06.012
And then compare it

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:07.480
to what one of her rivals.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.381
Vivek Ramaswamy,

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:10.350
another Republican candidate,

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.084
had to say about

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:12.352
what he thinks we should do.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:13.519
Vis-a-vis funding Ukraine.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:14.754
Here they were both yesterday

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.091
Ukraine has the

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.225
ability to win,

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.227
but we have to think bigger than that.

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:22.362
And for them to sit there

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:22.862
and say that

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.897
this is a territorial dispute

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.099
that's just not the case.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:27.900
To say that we should stay neutral.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.370
It is in the best interests of America.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.537
It's in the best interests

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.106
of our national security

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:34.307
for Ukraine to win.

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:35.541
We have to see this through.

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.110
We have to finish it.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.011
I do not think it is

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:40.046
a top foreign policy priority for us.

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:42.048
I don't think it is preferable for Russia

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:43.883
to be able to invade a sovereign country

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:44.984
that it's its neighbor

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.152
But I think the job of the US

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:47.086
president is to look

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:49.289
after American interests.

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:50.089
Not only did

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.357
she distinguish herself from him,

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:53.226
she distinguish herself on this issue

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:54.827
from Donald Trump.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:55.662
And from at least

00:04:55.662 --> 00:04:56.929
where Ron DeSantis was

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.798
when Tucker Carlson asked him about it.

00:04:58.798 --> 00:04:59.198
Yeah, it's

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:00.500
a clear eyed position

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.467
about the need

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.602
for the United States

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:04.604
to help the Ukrainians repel

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:05.738
this Russian invasion.

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:07.307
What we didn't play for Ramaswamy

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:08.007
is he went further.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.075
He said We have to end the war

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:11.544
by making major concession

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:12.912
territory to the Russians,

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:14.180
which is I mean, this is like

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:14.714
you know,

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:16.983
sort of pathetic dorm room debater crap.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.951
She had a real clear

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:19.786
eyed position

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:21.788
about what's in the best interests and

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:24.090
and whether this position is the

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.359
biggest issue in the primary or not.

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:27.894
The fact that someone is saying it out

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:29.095
loud and making the case

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:29.929
to the American people, like,

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.297
we got to win this thing.

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:32.265
That is a good thing.

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:33.499
And I'm glad she did that.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:34.667
She was very clear.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:35.635
She was very good.

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:36.169
The problem

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:38.438
that Nikki Haley is going to have is that

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:39.439
is the Republican Party

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:40.740
where she is right now

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:41.507
because she sounded

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:42.909
a lot like Lindsey Graham.

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:45.578
She sounded a lot like George W Bush.

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:46.946
They just elected Donald Trump,

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:48.881
which is the antithesis to everybody

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:49.849
I just named.

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:51.918
And so Ron DeSantis

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:54.187
