00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.488
Haley and Donald Trump

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:55.988
on that stage

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:57.090
on the issue of foreign policy.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.524
He just does not have the depth.

00:05:58.524 --> 00:05:59.325
You saw it in the Tucker

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:00.360
Carlson interview.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.028
But Nikki Haley did show she can debate.

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:02.995
I think the problem is

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:03.996
where is the majority

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:05.598
of maybe not Republicans,

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:07.500
but the Republican voting base?

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.401
I think that's interesting

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:09.902
because as you pointed out, Bakari,

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:12.004
leaning into foreign policy

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:12.772
and her strength there

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:13.473
because of her time,

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:14.874
of course, with the U.N.,

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:16.142
is that a top issue

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.877
